So this is just a quick way so that it executes the command on play.

22
00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:36.460
And you can see that when we start we can actually see our navigation at that point.

23
00:02:37.759 --> 00:02:43.360
OK, so we have other options when it comes to our nav mesh modifier.

24
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.360
So if we select the modifier that we have, and let's have a look at the details panel,

25
00:02:48.159 --> 00:02:54.719
you can see that the area class that we have, the area nav area is underscore null.

26
00:02:55.439 --> 00:03:00.479
Now, if you do a drop down, you can see that we have a few different options.

27
00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:03.840
We have obstacle, low height and null.

28
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.960
So low height, this works with the crouch ability.

29
00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:14.000
It means they're going to have to crouch in order to pass by.

30
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.879
And the one I want to go into is obstacle.

31
00:03:18.419 --> 00:03:24.990
Now, with the obstacle, you're going to see that the area is turned to...

32
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.509
It's suddenly changed to a different colour.

33
00:03:28.509 --> 00:03:31.229
So it's changed to a sort of orange colour.

34
00:03:31.789 --> 00:03:37.949
Now, if I drag, if I reduce that down in width, so I'm looking for...

35
00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.349
I change that to 0.4.

36
00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:48.080
Right, now we can see that when we're playing, the character is going to avoid this.

37
00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:58.539
Again, it works like a null one, but we're capable of, if we were to...

38
00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:05.490
I'm going to grab my major, my main one.

39
00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:07.250
I'm going to reduce that down in size.

40
00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.669
So that.

41
00:04:11.389 --> 00:04:16.699
Now, if you start, even though it's an obstacle, they are going to pass through it.

42
00:04:16.699 --> 00:04:21.259
But they're only going to pass through it if they have no other option to pass through it.

43
00:04:21.259 --> 00:04:22.139
So this is great.

44
00:04:22.139 --> 00:04:25.180
Say, for example, you have a pond or something like that,

45
00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:29.100
where normally a character would never walk through the pond.

46
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.579
But if it was the only way to get to the central island and you told them to get there,

47
00:04:33.579 --> 00:04:36.139
then it would pass through that area.

48
00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:45.009
However, what if you want to create an area which doesn't completely block them,

49
00:04:45.009 --> 00:04:47.009
but something like, I don't know, grass.

50
00:04:47.009 --> 00:04:51.250
If you had an urban scene and you want people to walk on the streets,

51
00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.329
but you didn't want them to walk on the grass.

52
00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:58.689
Or say you had an area that had tar in it that slowed people down or something like that.

53
00:04:58.689 --> 00:05:04.610
And you wanted that to be taken into consideration with the NavMesh.

54
00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:11.860
Now, what you could do then is we've got our NavMesh modifier here,

55
00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.279
and we got the selections of these ones.

56
00:05:15.279 --> 00:05:18.000
You can actually go away and create your own.

57
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:24.720
So if I was to right-hand click and select the Blueprint class

58
00:05:25.439 --> 00:05:32.319
and search for NavArea class, I think.

59
00:05:32.319 --> 00:05:33.040
Yes.

60
00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.720
OK, so here we go. NavArea.

61
00:05:35.279 --> 00:05:35.519
Right.

62
00:05:35.519 --> 00:05:38.079
So if we start with the NavArea as the top one,

63
00:05:38.079 --> 00:05:40.319
we've got these numbers and ones below it.

64
00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.120
If I was to select the NavArea,

65
00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:54.350
and I call this NavArea, NavArea underscore grass.

66
00:05:57.199 --> 00:06:04.769
So if I double click on that, you'll see that we have our own setup here.

67
00:06:05.329 --> 00:06:11.389
Now we don't actually have any override functionality in this at all.

68
00:06:11.389 --> 00:06:14.269
So you don't really want to be coding anything in this.

69
00:06:14.269 --> 00:06:18.029
What we care about is the class defaults here.

70
00:06:18.819 --> 00:06:23.620
So you can see we've got a couple of settings at the default cost.

71
00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:29.860
So at the moment, this is one, and we've got the fixed area entering costs.

72
00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:35.300
So what you could either do is you could create a one for a path,

73
00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:39.060
which has a lower cost, so that would encourage people to use that path.

74
00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:43.379
Or you could create one that is higher.

75
00:06:43.379 --> 00:06:44.899
In this case, that's what we're going to do.

76
00:06:44.899 --> 00:06:47.620
We're going to create one default cost of two.

77
00:06:48.339 --> 00:06:51.620
And it has a fixed area entering cost as well.

78
00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:57.459
So we could have it that there is a 0.5 cost to just entering the area.

79
00:06:57.459 --> 00:07:04.019
So this means that now walking through that is going to cost twice as much.

80
00:07:05.949 --> 00:07:11.149
So if I jump back in and I grab our NavModifier volume,

81
00:07:11.149 --> 00:07:13.790
you'll see in the drop down box, I now have grass.

82
00:07:14.509 --> 00:07:16.269
OK, and that's in pink.

83
00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:21.420
Now let's try this now.

84
00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.699
So I've got my character.

85
00:07:24.699 --> 00:07:29.019
If I move down to the bottom and I click on the other side,

86
00:07:29.019 --> 00:07:31.579
he's going to walk across because he does the maths,

87
00:07:31.579 --> 00:07:34.300
and it's going to be cheaper to walk across here

88
00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.660
than it will be to go all the way around from the other side.

89
00:07:38.879 --> 00:07:43.439
OK, however, if he comes over to the side here,

90
00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.480
and let's get closer, he's going to walk around

91
00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.480
because it's actually going to calculate to be cheaper for him.

92
00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.959
He's going to respect and he's not going to tread on the grass.

93
00:07:55.680 --> 00:08:00.800
So you can see we can just create a modifier

94
00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:05.040
which will slightly adapt the changes and how the character moves.

95
00:08:06.189 --> 00:08:12.990
So let's have a quick look at the NamMeshBounds volume.

96
00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:21.870
Let's have a look at the recast and you'll see if I click on the costs,

97
00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:31.870
draw polygon costs, you can see that we have a fixed cost of 2 plus 0.5 for entering.

98
00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:35.470
So everything around the outside is at 1.

99
00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:41.230
However, this is a slightly higher cost because we've created this NavMeshModifier.

100
00:08:41.789 --> 00:08:47.710
So that's a useful tool where you can update how the paths are calculated

101
00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:51.230
based on specific areas.

102
00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:57.870
And this is quite nice as well to make navigation look more natural,

103
00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:01.549
but also to split up mobs as they're moving around.

104
00:09:02.429 --> 00:09:04.750
They can choose different paths accordingly.

105
00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.190
OK, so that are your options.

106
00:09:08.669 --> 00:09:12.669
Your NavMeshModifier can block an area.

107
00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:16.429
We could create one that makes it cheaper.

108
00:09:16.429 --> 00:09:20.669
We could create one that tells them it is a low height

109
00:09:20.669 --> 00:09:22.750
and wouldn't be able to come through.

110
00:09:23.389 --> 00:09:28.029
And you can create an obstacle which it will only cross if it has to.

111
00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:30.559
OK, thanks a lot.

